        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 25 at 2:43PM PDT until September 25 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS Pendleton OR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Southwest to west winds 20 to 35 mph with gusts of 40 to 55
mph expected.

* WHERE...Eastern Columbia River Gorge of Oregon and Washington,
Foothills of the Blue Mountains of Oregon, Lower Columbia Basin of
Oregon, North Central Oregon, Yakima Valley, and Simcoe Highlands.

* WHEN...Until 11 PM PDT this evening.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Strongest winds are expected in the afternoon
and early evening.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.

Secure outdoor objects.

Patchy blowing dust may reduce visibility. Use caution if traveling
and be ready for a sudden drop in visibility if you encounter blowing
dust.</instruction>
